CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Each thread picks an element by a nondeterministic index and updates it
under that element's own mutex; the thread does it through `p = &a[i]`.
`p->datum++` is lowered to a store `with(a[i], datum, ...)` whose base
`a[i]` is a load at a symbolic index from an array still in symbol form.
Field sensitivity expanded that array with the plain path guard, so the
thread was recorded as reading every element, and paired, on the element it
did not touch, with main's update of it under the other mutex. Each element
is now read only under `i == k`.

Reported FAILED before the fix, SUCCESSFUL after. Reduced from goblint
06-symbeq_06-tricky_address1, which the fix also corrects, with _07 and _08.

See `array_element_pointer_load_race`: the thread always takes a[0]'s
mutex, so with `i == 1` it really races with main, and must stay FAILED.
